// Your displays. Without a block here niri gives each display its preferred mode and a fitting scale.
// To pin one, uncomment and adapt (names and modes: `niri msg outputs`), e.g. a 2880x1800 panel at 1.5,
// which makes a 1920x1200 workspace:
//
// output "eDP-1" {
//     mode "2880x1800@120.000"
//     scale 1.5
//     // VRR only kicks in for windows with `variable-refresh-rate true` (see rules.kdl).
//     variable-refresh-rate on-demand=true
// }
//
// Keep Serpantinum's Settings → Display scale at the same value (it re-applies its own at login).
// The glass installer writes this file only when it is missing and never changes it afterwards.
